From 971c478da7a3e47a498f3b566f8d533f62abab11 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Eden (Doris) build" <doris@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:44:19 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 40/49] Eden (Doris): texture cleanup without GPU waits; fewer
 worker wake-ups; redundant barriers skipped; hitch report

- Texture cleanup (setting, default Doris; "Eden" = build 15 behaviour): textures the GPU drew
  into are copied back without waiting for the GPU and removed at a later frame once the copy
  is done (called off if the texture was used, drawn into or written by the CPU meanwhile);
  textures stay 300 frames below a 2.2 GiB pressure threshold (Eden: 50 frames below 1.6 GiB,
  never removing GPU drawings), Eden's rules above it.
- Work is handed to the Vulkan worker every 16 draws instead of 4 (submit timing unchanged).
- A full barrier with nothing recorded since the previous one is skipped.
- Performance report: redundant barriers skipped, removals called off, and the longest
  hitches of each window with the GPU thread's CPU time, waits and work in that frame.

